## 6. Pipeline wiring (how it all runs on create)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` defines the `POST /api/owners` step order:
`validate` (RequireOwnerFields) → `postcode` (RequirePostcode) → `email` (NormaliseEmail) → `identity` (RequireUniqueIdentity) → `capacity` (RequireCityCapacity) → `dailyLimit` (RequireDailyCapacity) → `build` (BuildOwner) → **`customerCode` (AssignCustomerCode)** → `namesakes` (CountNamesakes) → `save` (SaveOwner, emits audit) → `respond` (RespondWithOwnerCreated). Steps from `identity` onward run under a `transaction` governance.

So on the write path only `customerCode` and `namesakeCount` are persisted onto the Owner; `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `contactPreference`, `displayName` are all derived read-only fields computed in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` when responding/fetching.

