- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RequireUniqueIdentity.java` — duplicate check on telephone.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` and `RespondWithOwner.java` — call `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` (triggering all the derived fields).

## OpenAPI field contract
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2089-2144 document the read-only fields: `customerCode` (described as `LAST3-NNNN`, example `SMI-0007`), `checkDigit` (Luhn 0-9), `householdId`, `identityKey`, `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`, example `SMI-0007-M26`), `namesakeCount`, `membershipLevel` (1-3), `locality` (region or `UNKNOWN`), `contactPreference`. Postcode input is documented at lines 2040-2042.

## Key discrepancy to flag
Three sources disagree on the `customerCode` format:
1. Current code (`AssignCustomerCode`): `CITY3-LAST3-NNNN` (per-city sequence).
2. OpenAPI doc: `LAST3-NNNN` (global sequence), example `SMI-0007`.
3. New acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash`): `<REGION>-<HASH8>` matching `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`.

The redesign target (per the test + `AcceptanceBase.shaHex`/`region` helpers) is `region(city)` + `-` + first-8-upper-hex of SHA-256. `AssignCustomerCode` is the single place to change; downstream `CheckDigit` (Luhn over digits — note a hex-hash code may contain few/no decimal digits) and `MembershipNumber` both consume `customerCode` and would be affected.

